      "body": "\r\nThis PR fixes the GPU HBM memory leak during `sleep-mode` when running multimodal models loaded with `--mm-encoder-tp-mode data` (Issue #47654).\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nWhen running sleep-mode transitions, vLLM offloads/remaps tracked memory blocks. However, during model warming and capture, both decoder and encoder CUDA graphs (the latter of which contains static input/output buffers for the vision encoder in DP mode) are captured outside of any active memory pool context. As a result, the memory allocated for these graphs is not registered in the allocator's tracker (`pointer_to_data`), causing them to leak on sleep and block multi-container sleep-swap.\r\n\r\nThis PR implements a `reuse_memory_pool` context manager for the allocator and wraps the persistent CUDA graph capture logic in `capture_model()` with the `\"weights\"` memory pool so that the allocations are tracked, offloaded, and remapped correctly during sleep/wake cycles.\r\n\r\nCloses #47654\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n*   **vllm/device_allocator/__init__.py**: Added `reuse_memory_pool` signature to `MemAllocator` protocol.\r\n*   **vllm/device_allocator/cumem.py**: Implemented `reuse_memory_pool` context manager for `CuMemAllocator`.\r\n*   **vllm/device_allocator/xpumem.py**: Implemented `reuse_memory_pool` context manager for `XpuMemAllocator`.\r\n*   **vllm/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py**: Implemented `_maybe_reuse_memory_pool_context` helper and wrapped the CUDA graph capture block in `capture_model` to reuse the `\"weights\"` memory pool.\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 4,
